Just my $0.02 about mapping the keyboard on PC nethack......not possible
using the previously mentioned command: rem <esc>[...etc, etc.

The command to use is:

prompt $e[key1;key2;13p

where key1 is the ASCII code of the key to be changed, and key2 is the ASCII
code to which key1 must change to. Extended ASCII codes can be accessed and
changed as well. In fact if key2 is in quotation marks, key1 can be issued
whole words like "Elbereth" (ie. in one keystroke Elbereth can be entered).
The ;13p simply issues a return after the key has been issued from the keyboard.

The catch....you need ANSI.sys (but then again who doesn't play nethack without
it?), AND this whole darned idea DOESN'T work!

SO....scrap the idea of remapping <shift-q> to another location.....NETHACK
overrides all prompt commands previously issued.

frog.

btw. the 'rem' command previously given to us (4-5 messages before this one)
     simply means remark.....
